CREA v3  —  n8n Hands Layer
3.0.0 · 2026-09-09

A standalone, self-healing WhatsApp AI booking assistant + shoot-ops automations, run by
the owner on their own Mac and their own accounts.

Install:  INSTALL.md         (one-time setup, ~1 hour — mostly account signups + downloads)
Operate:  OPERATIONS.md      (changes, updates, features, backup, recovery — day two onward)
Resilience & security:  COUNTERMEASURES.md
Deploy:   ./go-live.sh       (Docker Compose — n8n + WAHA + vault-api, one command)

What v3 adds over v2
- Resilience: an LLM circuit breaker + optional second endpoint (crea-llm), Docker
  healthchecks, and a host watchdog (launchd) that restarts a down/wedged container,
  re-links a dropped WhatsApp session, prunes disk, and pages the owner for what it can't fix.
- Security: an injection-hardened prompt PLUS a deterministic reply guard on every message
  (strips an invented price, softens a booking confirmation, blocks prompt leakage);
  per-sender rate limiting; a blocklist; input size caps; group/status/media filtered out.
- Observability: a health endpoint + dashboard (localhost:5692/status.html), a richer
  ./go-live.sh --status, a daily self-check that pages on real problems (deduped), a
  system-health line in the morning briefing, deduped incident logging.
- Backup/restore built in: ./go-live.sh --backup / --restore / --export.

14 workflows. Verified end to end against a live model on n8n 2.30.7 — see TEST-REPORT.md,
including the failure and attack cases.
